---
title: "Drawbridge — Event backbone: agents react to events, they never poll"
---
flowchart LR
  subgraph PUB["PUBLISHERS"]
    direction TB
    DASHP["Dashboard"]
    PORTAL["Vendor portal"]
    INBOX["Inbox service"]
    ARMORP["Armor pipeline"]
    SCHED["Cloud Scheduler"]
  end

  subgraph TOPICS["PUB/SUB TOPICS"]
    direction TB
    T1["review.intake"]
    T2["review.plan_ready"]
    T3["vendor.reply_received"]
    T4["vendor.evidence_uploaded"]
    T5["evidence.screened"]
    T6["review.findings_ready"]
    T7["review.score_ready"]
    T8["review.approved"]
    T9["watchdog.hit"]
    T10["watchdog.sweep<br/><i>scheduled trigger</i>"]
    T11["review.rescore<br/><i>raised by adversarial conduct</i>"]
  end

  subgraph SUB["CONSUMERS — every one idempotent, because delivery is at-least-once"]
    direction TB
    O["Orchestrator"]
    Q["Questionnaire"]
    E["Evidence"]
    R["Risk Scorer"]
    W["Watchdog"]
  end

  ENV["<b>EventEnvelope</b> — one shape for every message<br/>event_id · type · review_id<br/><b>idem_key</b> = review_id, plan_vN and step_id<br/><b>trace_id</b> ties the event to its span tree<br/>source · ts · payload<br/><br/>this uniformity is what makes tracing,<br/>replay and idempotency work at all"]
  DLQ["<b>Dead letter after five delivery attempts</b><br/>the review moves to NEEDS_HUMAN and surfaces<br/>as a dashboard card — visible failure handling<br/>is a graded behaviour, so make it visible"]
  ACK["Ack deadline 60s, extended explicitly<br/>for long model calls"]
  ORDER["<b>At-least-once — and NO ordering guarantee</b><br/>duplicates are handled by the idempotency key; <i>sequence</i> is handled here.<br/>Every consumer checks review state before acting: a reply after SCORED attaches<br/>as an addendum and reopens the score; evidence.screened before a plan parks and<br/>retries; watchdog.hit deduplicates on signal id; any event for a DECIDED review<br/>appends and never mutates. A decided review is immutable."]

